From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 10:18:08 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 174/192] wifi: ath11k: nss: pass the real ath11k_base to the
 wifili ext callback

999-904 wrapped ath11k_nss_wifili_ext_callback_fn() to avoid a function
pointer cast, but it gets ab back with netdev_priv(netdev). The "netdev"
is not a net_device: ath11k_nss_init() registers the wifili interface
with ab itself, and qca-nss-drv hands that pointer back unchanged
(nss_core.c: ext_cb(ndev, ...), ndev being the registered pointer).
netdev_priv() therefore points into the middle of ab, and the callback
ran with a bogus ab.

Only the TKIP MIC-error branch acts on it: ath11k_nss_process_mic_error()
looks up peers and takes locks through ab. The other packet types reach
an ath11k_dbg(), which reads ab only in ATH11K_DEBUG builds; on a busy
channel that is about ten invalid-peer broadcasts a second.

Use the pointer as registered. Issue #22.
---
 drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
index 28f3437..536f76c 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -525,10 +525,9 @@ static inline void ath11k_nss_wifili_ext_callback_wrapper(struct net_device *net
 						   struct sk_buff *skb,
 						   struct napi_struct *napi)
 {
-	// Retrieve the ath11k_base from the net_device's private data
-	struct ath11k_base *ab = (struct ath11k_base *)netdev_priv(netdev);
+	/* nss_register_wifili_if() was given ab itself as the "netdev" */
+	struct ath11k_base *ab = (struct ath11k_base *)netdev;
 
-	// Call the original function with the retrieved ath11k_base
 	ath11k_nss_wifili_ext_callback_fn(ab, skb, napi);
 }
 
